statement:
Let n ∈ ℕ, let F : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ be C¹ and let V ⊆ ℝ^{n+1} be open. Then there are open sets Ω_k ⊆ ℝ^{n+1} and maps Θ_k : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ^{n+1} (k ∈ ℕ) such that, for every k, all of the following hold:
- Θ_k is C¹ on Ω_k and injective on Ω_k;
- DΘ_k(z) is injective for every z ∈ Ω_k;
- Θ_k(Ω_k) is open and contained in V;
- F(Θ_k(z)) = z_0 for every z ∈ Ω_k.
Moreover every y ∈ V with DF(y) ≠ 0 lies in ⋃_k Θ_k(Ω_k).
